<article class="env-lemma" id="00NE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00NE">Lemma <span data-tag="00NE">10.104.8</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian local Cohen-Macaulay ring of dimension $d$. Let $0 \to K \to R^{\oplus n} \to M \to 0$ be an exact sequence of $R$-modules. Then either $M = 0$, or $\text{depth}(K) > \text{depth}(M)$, or $\text{depth}(K) = \text{depth}(M) = d$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/00LX" data-tag="00LX">10.72.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>